    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "Young people's experiences with electrical infrastructures and power outages were analyzed using mixed qualitative and quantitative data in \"Electric Youth: Young People, Energy Infrastructures, and Power Cuts\". \"Discovering Governing Spatial Interaction Equations in Dynamic Urban Systems\" introduces U-Discovery, a framework that combines spatial differential equation formalisms, Large Language Model hypothesis generation, and neural parameter fitting to discover governing equations for dynamic urban systems. Finally, \"Measuring Research Convergence in Interdisciplinary Teams Using Large Language Models and Graph Analytics\" presents a multi-layer computational framework combining large language models, graph analytics, and expert validation to track how interdisciplinary team members align their ideas over time.",
